<h1>GisTV Privacy Policy</h1>

<p class="updated"><strong>Last updated:</strong> September 20, 2026</p>

<p>
GisTV ("GisTV", "we", "us", or "our") is an application provided by GIS.
This Privacy Policy explains how information may be handled when you use the
GisTV Android TV application.
</p>

<h2>1. Information You Provide</h2>

<p>
Depending on the features you use, GisTV may process information that you
provide directly, such as your name, email address, account information,
playlist information, or other information necessary to provide requested
features.
</p>

<h2>2. Device and Technical Information</h2>

<p>
GisTV may process technical information associated with your device when
necessary to operate, secure, synchronize, troubleshoot, or improve the
application. This may include device or installation identifiers, application
version information, operating-system information, network information, and
diagnostic information.
</p>

<p>
GisTV does not require access to information unrelated to the functionality
of the application.
</p>

<h2>3. Account and Synchronization Features</h2>

<p>
If you use account or synchronization features, information associated with
those features may be transmitted between the application and the services
used to provide them. The information processed depends on the features you
choose to use.
</p>

<p>
Synchronization is intended to allow supported Gis applications and devices
to maintain the information necessary for the enabled synchronization
features.
</p>

<h2>4. Playlists and IPTV Information</h2>

<p>
If you configure IPTV or playlist features, GisTV may process information
required to retrieve and display the content or services you configure.
This may include playlist addresses, channel information, provider
information, authentication information, and related configuration data,
depending on the service you use.
</p>

<p>
GisTV does not control the privacy practices of third-party IPTV providers,
playlist providers, streaming services, or websites that you choose to
access through the application. You should review the privacy policies of
those services separately.
</p>

<h2>5. Analytics, Advertising, and Diagnostics</h2>

<p>
GisTV may use technical diagnostics or similar services when required to
operate and maintain the application. If third-party analytics, crash
reporting, or advertising services are enabled in a particular version of
GisTV, those services may process information according to their own privacy
policies.
</p>

<p>
GisTV does not sell your personal information.
</p>

<h2>6. How Information Is Used</h2>

<p>Information may be used to:</p>

<ul>
  <li>provide and operate GisTV features;</li>
  <li>authenticate and manage accounts;</li>
  <li>provide supported synchronization features;</li>
  <li>retrieve and display configured IPTV content;</li>
  <li>maintain application security;</li>
  <li>diagnose technical problems;</li>
  <li>respond to support requests; and</li>
  <li>comply with applicable legal requirements.</li>
</ul>

<h2>7. Data Retention</h2>

<p>
Information is retained only for as long as reasonably necessary to provide
the applicable features, maintain security, comply with legal obligations,
resolve disputes, and enforce applicable agreements.
</p>

<h2>8. Data Deletion</h2>

<p>
Where GisTV provides an account or data-deletion feature, users may request
deletion of their account and associated personal information through the
available account or support mechanisms.
</p>

<p>
Some information may need to be retained when required by law, necessary
for security, or required to complete legitimate business or technical
operations.
</p>

<h2>9. Third-Party Services</h2>

<p>
GisTV may interact with third-party services selected or configured by the
user. Those services operate under their own terms and privacy policies.
GisTV is not responsible for the privacy practices of third-party services
that users choose to access.
</p>

<h2>10. Security</h2>

<p>
We use reasonable technical and organizational measures intended to protect
information processed through GisTV. However, no method of transmission or
electronic storage can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
</p>

<h2>11. Children's Privacy</h2>

<p>
GisTV is not intended to knowingly collect personal information from
children in violation of applicable law. If you believe that a child has
provided personal information improperly, please contact us so that the
information can be reviewed and, where appropriate, deleted.
</p>

<h2>12. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

<p>
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The updated version
will be published at this location with a revised "Last updated" date.
</p>

